    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1993423530147369188",
      "url": "https://x.com/CreativeScty/status/1993423530147369188",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/CreativeScty/status/1993423530147369188",
      "text": "A Week of Global Cataclysms. And One Piece of News That Changes Everything\n\n🟢 https://t.co/wumGAfnE4D\n\n🔴 https://t.co/Y885RmYHyA\n\n🌪 A destructive EF-4 tornado, as if straight out of a Hollywood movie, hit the streets of the Brazilian city of Rio Bonito do Iguaçu, becoming the most powerful tornado in Brazil’s recent history. Winds of up to 300 km/h reduced entire neighborhoods to rubble, leaving around 1,000 residents homeless and claiming 6 lives.\n\n– A fire in Tongariro National Park destroyed 2,800 hectares in New Zealand;\n– Arctic cold struck the USA\n– Canada was hit by a rare early snowstorm \n– Japan experienced a series of 37 earthquakes in just over a day, including three powerful shocks with magnitudes above 6.0\n– Two massive typhoons struck the Philippines: Kalmaegi claimed 232 lives, and Fung-Wong killed another 25 people\n– Iran is enduring a historic drought\n– In China “Hunzi Cloud Bridge” collapsed\n\n#CreativeSociety",
